NextKey v2 — the full loop on Sepolia
=====================================
Run on 2026-09-06, evening (Europe/Zurich), against the ENSv2 hackathon
deployment. Every line below is from one uninterrupted session; nothing is
reconstructed and nothing is edited except the removal of blank lines.

What this run demonstrates: a secret stored under a scheme where the *record
name* of each grant is derived from an ECDH result rather than from the
recipient's public key. Sharing, opening as two different identities,
revocation, and the asymmetry that revocation is supposed to produce — one
identity loses access, the other does not.


